{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Behold I</b> — I will smite the seed so that it does not grow, because you have set My table empty." "<b>And your חגיכם</b> — like אסרו חג בעבותים (Psalms 118:27). The meaning of חגיכם is \"your offerings.\" I will scatter them on your faces. And the meaning of ארחיקכם מעל פני (I will distance you from My face) is that I will not see you." "<b>And I will carry you off</b> — the one who carries off is the enemy, about whom it says הנני שלח לכם (behold I send against you [the curse])."], :book :malachi, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {1 "Resolved וטעם ארחיקכם as introducing Ibn Ezra's reading of the phrase מפניכם וזריתי פרש in the verse, treating ארחיקכם מעל פני as his paraphrase of HaShem distancing them."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Malachi -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/malachi"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:12.321674455Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}